Description:

Incoming WebSocket messages are now bounded in size, both as received and
after permessage-deflate inflation.  For JMAP over WebSocket the bound is
:imapdconf:`jmap_max_size_request`; for other WebSocket channels it is
:imapdconf:`maxmessagesize`.  A message over the bound closes the connection
with a Message Too Big status.  Previously a small, highly compressed message
could be inflated without limit, exhausting the memory of the httpd process.


